{%- liquid
  # render arguments and tag filters do not mix, so the one translated string
  # this section owns is resolved up front. It is also the ONLY key here —
  # locales/en.default.json is owned elsewhere, so nothing new is invented and
  # homepage.coach.eyebrow keeps its single call site.
  assign coach_eyebrow = 'homepage.coach.eyebrow' | t
  assign coach_heading = section.settings.heading | default: 'Coaching that shows its work'
  assign coach_heading_id = 'CoachNotes-' | append: section.id
-%}

<section class="sl-coach" aria-labelledby="{{ coach_heading_id }}">
  <div class="sl-wrap sl-reveal">
    {%- comment -%}
      This used to open with the shared eyebrow → centred h2 → lede stack.
      So did the nine other homepage bands, and ten identical openings is
      exactly what made the page read as a brochure rather than a readout.
      The head is hand-rolled here: the mono label sits in a margin stub the
      way a spec sheet numbers its left column, the title and the lede take
      unequal columns beside it, and nothing is centred.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <header class="sl-coach__head">
      <div class="sl-coach__stub">
        <p class="sl-coach__kicker">{{ coach_eyebrow }}</p>
        {%- if section.settings.stub != blank -%}
          <p class="sl-coach__stub-note">{{ section.settings.stub }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
      <h2 id="{{ coach_heading_id }}" class="sl-coach__title">{{ coach_heading }}</h2>
      {%- if section.settings.sub != blank -%}
        <p class="sl-coach__lede">{{ section.settings.sub }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </header>

    {%- comment -%}
      A register, not a card grid. One column at every width, rows separated
      by the 1px-gap idiom — container painted --sl-border, each row painted
      --sl-bg-card — so what divides them is a hairline rule rather than a
      shadowed card edge. A drop shadow is invisible on this field anyway;
      the only cast that survives here is the inset lit edge below.

      These are product behaviours, never quotes, so nothing here is marked
      up as quoted speech and nothing is attributed to a person. Doing either
      would turn documented behaviour into a testimonial we cannot support —
      tests/test_premium_storefront.py greps this file to keep it that way,
      so do not reach for a quotation element even as a styling hook.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="sl-coach__register">
      {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
        {%- liquid
          # Zero-padded so the ordinals sit as an even two-character column
          # in the rail. max_blocks is 6, so the branch is the whole story.
          assign coach_index = forloop.index
          if coach_index < 10
            assign coach_index = coach_index | prepend: '0'
          endif
        -%}
        <article class="sl-coach__card"{{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
          <div class="sl-coach__rail">
            {%- comment -%}
              The ordinal is a register position, not content: it is hidden
              from assistive tech so a screen reader gets the label and the
              entry, not "zero one" before every one of them.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <span class="sl-coach__index" aria-hidden="true">{{ coach_index }}</span>
            {%- if block.settings.label != blank -%}
              {%- comment -%}
                This label used to be an amber chip. Amber marks a value the
                engine measured, and "CLUB CONTEXT" is the name of a
                behaviour, not a measurement — so it is bone mono now. The
                section carries neither signal colour for the same reason:
                nothing here was measured and nothing here reads live.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              <h3 class="sl-coach__label">{{ block.settings.label }}</h3>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
          <p class="sl-coach__quote">{{ block.settings.quote }}</p>
        </article>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>

    {%- if section.settings.footnote != blank -%}
      <p class="sl-coach__footnote sl-mono-label">{{ section.settings.footnote }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</section>

{% stylesheet %}
/* Full section rhythm rather than the compact rung: this is three long rows
   of prose, and running them tight against the neighbouring bands is what
   made the homepage scroll as one continuous stack of cards. */
.sl-coach {
  padding-top: var(--sl-section-space);
  padding-bottom: var(--sl-section-space);
  border-top: 1px solid var(--sl-border);
}

.sl-coach__head {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
  gap: var(--sl-space-5);
  margin: 0 0 clamp(32px, 4vw, 48px);
}
/* Capped so the rule under the margin note stays a stub. Below 1000px the
   head is one column, and without a measure that hairline would run the full
   page width and read as a section divider instead of a label underline. */
.sl-coach__stub {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: flex-start;
  gap: var(--sl-space-2);
  max-width: 34ch;
}
.sl-coach__kicker,
.sl-coach__stub-note {
  margin: 0;
  font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
  font-size: var(--sl-eyebrow-size);
  font-weight: 500;
  letter-spacing: var(--sl-eyebrow-track);
  line-height: 1.4;
  text-transform: uppercase;
}
/* The shared .sl-eyebrow paints itself amber, and amber is reserved for a
   value the engine measured — so this section spells its own kicker instead
   of borrowing a rule that would spend the signal on a section label. */
.sl-coach__kicker { color: var(--sl-ink-soft); }
.sl-coach__stub-note {
  align-self: stretch;
  padding-top: var(--sl-space-2);
  border-top: 1px solid var(--sl-border);
  color: var(--sl-ink-muted);
}
.sl-coach__title {
  margin: 0;
  max-width: 16ch;
  font-size: var(--sl-heading-support);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  text-align: left;
}
.sl-coach__lede {
  margin: 0;
  max-width: 46ch;
  color: var(--sl-ink-soft);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-lg);
  line-height: 1.55;
  text-wrap: pretty;
}

.sl-coach__register {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
  gap: 1px;
  background: var(--sl-border);
  border: 1px solid var(--sl-border);
}
.sl-coach__card {
  margin: 0;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: stretch;
  justify-content: flex-start;
  gap: var(--sl-space-4);
  padding: var(--sl-card-inset);
  background: var(--sl-bg-card);
  text-align: left;
}
/* The lit top edge from --sl-shadow-card, applied to the row that owns the
   register's top edge. It cannot go on the container: the rows paint their
   own background over an inset shadow, so it would never be seen. */
.sl-coach__card:first-child {
}

/* Below 560px the ordinal runs inline with the label — a phone should not
   spend a whole line on two characters. The rail becomes a column at 560. */
.sl-coach__rail {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: row;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  align-items: baseline;
  gap: var(--sl-space-3);
}
.sl-coach__index {
  font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-lg);
  font-weight: 500;
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  line-height: 1;
  color: var(--sl-ink-muted);
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}
/* An h3 inherits the expanded display face at 800 from base.css. DM Mono
   ships 400 and 500 only, so anything heavier would synthesize a fake bold
   — the family, weight and tracking are all restated deliberately. */
.sl-coach__label {
  margin: 0;
  font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
  font-weight: 500;
  letter-spacing: 0.16em;
  line-height: 1.4;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--sl-ink);
  text-wrap: pretty;
}
.sl-coach__quote {
  margin: 0;
  color: var(--sl-ink);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-base);
  line-height: 1.62;
  text-wrap: pretty;
}
.sl-coach__footnote {
  display: block;
  max-width: 60ch;
  margin: var(--sl-space-5) 0 0;
  text-align: left;
}

@media (min-width: 560px) {
  /* The row splits into a stub and its entry. gap drops to 0 because the
     column rule and its own padding now do the separating — a gap on top of
     a rule reads as two dividers for one boundary. */
  .sl-coach__card {
    flex-direction: row;
    gap: 0;
  }
  .sl-coach__rail {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    width: clamp(140px, 22%, 220px);
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: stretch;
    gap: var(--sl-space-3);
    padding-right: clamp(20px, 3vw, 32px);
  }
  .sl-coach__index {
    padding-bottom: var(--sl-space-2);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sl-border);
  }
  /* Decorative hairline, never a control edge — --sl-border is the right
     token for a column rule and the wrong one for anything clickable. */
  .sl-coach__quote {
    flex: 1 1 auto;
    padding-left: clamp(20px, 3vw, 32px);
    border-left: 1px solid var(--sl-border);
  }
}

@media (min-width: 1000px) {
  /* Three unequal columns — stub, title, lede — bottom-aligned so the mono
     margin note sits on the title's baseline rather than floating above it.
     The asymmetry is the whole point; nothing on this band is centred. */
  .sl-coach__head {
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 3fr) minmax(0, 5fr) minmax(0, 4fr);
    align-items: end;
    gap: clamp(32px, 3vw, 56px);
  }
  .sl-coach__rail { width: clamp(180px, 24%, 260px); }
}

@media (max-width: 749px) {
  /* A 16ch measure is a good column beside a lede and a bad one when it is
     the only thing on the line. */
  .sl-coach__title { max-width: 100%; }
}

/* No transitions, hovers or animations are declared anywhere above: nothing
   in this register is interactive, and a hover affordance on a row that
   cannot be clicked is a lie. There is consequently no motion for
   prefers-reduced-motion to switch off. */
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Coach notes",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Coaching that shows its work" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "stub", "label": "Margin note", "default": "WHAT THE REPORT DOES" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "sub", "label": "Subheading", "default": "The report keeps the decision legible: which club you filmed, which supported movement comes first, what to practice, and what must match on the next clip." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "footnote", "label": "Footnote", "default": "PRODUCT FEATURES SHOWN · NOT A CUSTOMER TESTIMONIAL" }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "note",
      "name": "Report note",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "label", "label": "Behaviour label", "default": "CLUB CONTEXT" },
        { "type": "textarea", "id": "quote", "label": "Card text", "default": "An iron and a driver ask different questions. Club selection is required before upload, stays attached to the report, and gives the next comparison the same equipment context." }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "max_blocks": 6,
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Coach notes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "note",
          "settings": {
            "label": "CLUB CONTEXT",
            "quote": "An iron and a driver ask different questions. Club selection is required before upload, stays attached to the report, and gives the next comparison the same equipment context."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "settings": {
            "label": "ONE PRIORITY",
            "quote": "Supported findings are ranked, then one movement is brought forward with a matching drill and pass mark, so the range session has one clear job instead of scattered advice."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "settings": {
            "label": "MATCHED RE-FILM",
            "quote": "Use the same club and selected view, then repeat the hip-height, full-body setup so the next clip can test whether the practiced movement held under comparable capture conditions."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
